{"cklb_version":"1.0","stigs":[{"display_name":"Adobe Acrobat Professional DC Continuous Track","release_info":"Release: 1 Benchmark Date: 23 Jul 2021","version":"2","rules":[{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bEnhancedSecurityStandalone == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21311700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bEnhancedSecurityStandalone == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21311700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bEnhancedSecurityStandalone'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\n                        : name equals 'bEnhancedSecurityStandalone'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous Enhanced Security for standalone mode must be enabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Enhanced Security (ES) is a sandbox capability that restricts access to system resources. ES can be configured in two modes: Standalone mode is when Acrobat opens the desktop PDF client. ES Browser mode is when a PDF is opened via the browser plugin. When Enhanced Security is enabled and a PDF file tries to complete a restricted action from an untrusted location, a security warning must appear.Enhanced Security âhardensâ the application against risky actions. It prevents cross domain access, prohibits script and data injection, blocks stream access to XObjects, silent printing, and execution of high privilege JavaScript.","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bEnhancedSecurityStandalone\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous  &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; 'Enable Enhanced Security Standalone' to 'Enabled'.\n","group_id":"V-213117","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":["SV-94065","V-79359"],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-213117","uuid":"73F2654F-6BF7-1014-B273-DF97757062CD","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213117","href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id":"SV-213117r766511","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-213117r766511_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUtilizing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bEnhancedSecurityStandalone\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for bEnhancedSecurityStandalone is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nGUI path: Edit &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; In the 'Enhanced Security' section&gt; Verify 'Enable Enhanced Security' checkbox is checked and greyed out (locked).  If the box is not checked nor greyed out (locked), this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; 'Enable Enhanced Security Standalone' must be set to 'Enabled'.\n\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-213117","title":"SRG-APP-000112"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"3973","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"AADC-CN-000205","ccis":["CCI-001695","CCI-002530"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000112"},{"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213118"},"uuid":"73F271EC-6BF7-1014-AE27-C2BF0E3067CE","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bEnhancedSecurityInBrowser\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; 'Enable Enhanced Security In Browser' to 'Enabled'.\n\n\n","legacy_ids":["SV-94067","V-79361"],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-213118","group_id":"V-213118","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","discussion":"Enhanced Security (ES) is a sandbox capability that restricts access to system resources and prevents PDF cross domain access. ES can be configured in two modes: Standalone mode is when Acrobat opens the desktop PDF client. ES Browser mode is when a PDF is opened via the browser plugin. When Enhanced Security is enabled and a PDF file tries to complete a restricted action from an untrusted location, a security warning must appear.Enhanced Security âhardensâ the application against risky actions. It prevents cross domain access, prohibits script and data injection, blocks stream access to XObjects, silent printing, and execution of high privilege JavaScript.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous Enhanced Security for browser mode must be enabled.","security_override_guidance":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bEnhancedSecurityInBrowser == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21311800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bEnhancedSecurityInBrowser == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21311800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bEnhancedSecurityInBrowser'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\n                        : name equals 'bEnhancedSecurityInBrowser'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-001695","CCI-002530"],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000112","severity":"medium","rule_version":"AADC-CN-000210","reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-213118","title":"SRG-APP-000112"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-213118r766514","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUtilizing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bEnhancedSecurityInBrowser\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for bEnhancedSecurityInBrowser is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; 'Enable Enhanced Security In Browser' must be set to 'Enabled'.\n","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213118r766514_rule"},{"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-213119","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213119r766517_rule","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUtilizing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: iFileAttachmentPerms\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for iFileAttachmentPerms is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nGUI path: Edit &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; In the 'PDF File Attachments' section &gt; Verify  'Allow opening of non-PDF file attachments with external applications' checkbox is unchecked and greyed out (locked).  If the box is checked and not greyed out (locked), this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; 'Allow opening of non-PDF file attachments with external applications' must be set to 'Disabled'.\n","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-213119r766517","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"AADC-CN-000275","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous PDF file attachments must be blocked.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Acrobat Pro allows for files to be attached to PDF documents. Attachments represent a potential security risk because they can contain malicious content, open other dangerous files, or launch applications.This feature prevents users from opening or launching file types other than PDF or FDF and disables the menu option to re-enable.","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (iFileAttachmentPerms == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21311900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : iFileAttachmentPerms == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21311900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'iFileAttachmentPerms'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\n                        : name equals 'iFileAttachmentPerms'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"73F27B41-6BF7-1014-88F0-D49509599D4A","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213119"},"group_id":"V-213119","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":["SV-94069","V-79363"],"group_id_src":"V-213119","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: iFileAttachmentPerms\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; 'Allow opening of non-PDF file attachments with external applications' to 'Disabled'.\n\n"},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","rule_version":"AADC-CN-000280","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-213120"},"reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213120r766520","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-213120r766520_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUtilizing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cDefaultLaunchURLPerms\\\n\nValue Name: iUnknownURLPerms\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 3\n\nIf the value for iUnknownURLPerms is not set to â3â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nGUI path: Edit &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; In the 'Internet Access from PDF Files outside the web browser' section &gt; Select 'Change Settings' option &gt;  In the 'PDF Files may connect to web sites to share or get information' section, if 'Block PDF files access to all web sites' is selected and greyed out (locked), then this is not a finding. If 'Custom setting' is checked, then in the 'Default behavior for web sites that are not in the above list' section,  verify the radio button 'Block access'  is checked and greyed out (locked) .  If the box is not checked nor greyed out, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; 'Access to unknown websites' must be set to 'Enabled' and 'Block access' selected in the drop down box.\n","uuid":"73F2843A-6BF7-1014-A595-A4D997C74577","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213120","href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cDefaultLaunchURLPerms\\\n\nValue Name: iUnknownURLPerms\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 3\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; 'Access to unknown websites' to 'Enabled' and select 'Block access' in the drop down box.\n","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-213120","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":["SV-94071","V-79365"],"group_id_src":"V-213120","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous access to unknown websites must be restricted.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Acrobat provides the ability for the user to store a list of websites with an associated behavior of allow, ask, or block. Websites that are not in this list are unknown. PDF files can contain URLs that will initiate connections to unknown websites in order to share or get information. That access must be restricted.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (iUnknownURLPerms == 3)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21312000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : iUnknownURLPerms == 3\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21312000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cDefaultLaunchURLPerms'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'iUnknownURLPerms'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000003 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cDefaultLaunchURLPerms'\n                        : name equals 'iUnknownURLPerms'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (iURLPerms == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21312100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : iURLPerms == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21312100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cDefaultLaunchURLPerms'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'iURLPerms'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cDefaultLaunchURLPerms'\n                        : name equals 'iURLPerms'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous access to websites must be blocked.","mitigations":"","discussion":"PDF files can contain URLs that initiate connections to websites in order to share or get information. Any Internet access introduces a security risk as malicious websites can transfer harmful content or silently gather data.","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","group_id":"V-213121","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":["SV-94073","V-79367"],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-213121","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cDefaultLaunchURLPerms\\\n\nValue Name: iURLPerms\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nThe setting may be set to \"0\" if a documented risk acceptance approving the websites is approved by the ISSO/AO.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; 'Access to websites' to 'Enabled' and select 'Block PDF files access to all web sites' in the drop down box.  Select 'Custom setting' if needed and provide a documented risk acceptance approved by the ISSO/AO approving the websites. \n\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"73F28C1E-6BF7-1014-849B-B765ED25E398","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213121"},"rule_id_src":"SV-213121r766523_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUtilizing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cDefaultLaunchURLPerms\\\n\nValue Name: iURLPerms\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for iURLPerms is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nSetting the value for iURLPerms to \"0\" means that a custom settings has been selected.  Custom setting allows for specific websites to be used for PDF workflows.  These websites must be approved by the ISSO/AO otherwise the setting must be \"1\" which blocks access to all websites.  If the iURLPerms setting is \"0\" and a documented risk acceptance approving the websites is provided, this is not a finding.\n\nGUI path: Edit &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; In the 'Internet Access from PDF Files outside the web browser' section &gt; Select 'Change Settings' option &gt; In the 'PDF Files may connect to web sites to share or get information' section &gt; Verify the radio button 'Block PDF files access to all web sites' is selected and greyed out (locked).    If 'Custom setting' is checked, a documented risk acceptance approved by the ISSO/AO approving the websites must be provided and then this is not a finding. \n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; 'Access to websites' must be set to 'Enabled' and 'Block PDF files access to all web sites' selected in the drop down box. If 'Custom setting' is selected, a documented risk acceptance approved by the ISSO/AO approving the websites must be provided and then this is not a finding. \n\n\n","rule_id":"SV-213121r766523","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-213121"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"3973","third_party_tools":"","rule_version":"AADC-CN-000285","severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","ccis":["CCI-000381"]},{"rule_version":"AADC-CN-000290","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id_src":"SV-213122r766526_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bEnableFlash\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0\n\nIf the value for bEnableFlash is not set to â0â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Enable Flash' must be set to 'Disabled'.\n","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-213122r766526","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-213122"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"3973","third_party_tools":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":["SV-94075","V-79369"],"group_id_src":"V-213122","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-213122","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bEnableFlash\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Enable Flash' to 'Disabled'.\n\n","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213122","href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml"},"uuid":"73F29594-6BF7-1014-94DA-F28C5C470CD3","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bEnableFlash == 0)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21312200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bEnableFlash == 0\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21312200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bEnableFlash'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\n                        : name equals 'bEnableFlash'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Flash has a long history of vulnerabilities.  Although Flash is no longer provided with Acrobat, if the system has Flash installed, a malicious PDF could execute code on the system.  Configuring Flash to run from a privileged location limits the execution capability of untrusted Flash content that may be embedded in the PDF.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous must be configured to block Flash Content.","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C"},{"group_tree":{"id":"V-213123","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-213123r766529","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213123r766529_rule","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nNote: The Key Name \"cCloud\" is not created by default in the Acrobat Pro DC install and must be created.\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cCloud\n\nValue Name: bAdobeSendPluginToggle\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for bAdobeSendPluginToggle is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Send and Track plugin' must be set to 'Disabled'.\n","ia_controls":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","rule_version":"AADC-CN-000295","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","mitigations":"","discussion":"When enabled, the Adobe Send and Track button appears in Outlook. When an email is composed it enables the ability to send large files as public links through Outlook. The attached files can be uploaded to the Adobe Document Cloud and public links to the files are inserted in the email body.","rule_title":"The Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous Send and Track plugin for Outlook must be disabled.","security_override_guidance":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bAdobeSendPluginToggle == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21312300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bAdobeSendPluginToggle == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21312300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cCloud'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bAdobeSendPluginToggle'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cCloud'\n                        : name equals 'bAdobeSendPluginToggle'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213123"},"uuid":"73F29DA8-6BF7-1014-B79B-B80D94D8EF2D","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nNote: The Key Name \"cCloud\" is not created by default in the Acrobat Pro DC install and must be created.\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cCloud\n\nValue Name: bAdobeSendPluginToggle\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Send and Track plugin' to 'Disabled'.\n\n","legacy_ids":["SV-94077","V-79371"],"group_id_src":"V-213123","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-213123","potential_impacts":""},{"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-213124","title":"SRG-APP-000380"},"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bDisableTrustedFolders\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for bDisableTrustedFolders is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nGUI path: Edit &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; In the 'Privileged Locations' section, verify 'Add Folder Path' option is greyed out (locked).  If this option is not greyed out, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; 'Privileged folder locations' must be set to 'Disabled'. \n\n","rule_id_src":"SV-213124r766532_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-213124r766532","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"group_title":"SRG-APP-000380","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-001813"],"rule_version":"AADC-CN-000840","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous privileged file and folder locations must be disabled.","discussion":"Privileged Locations are the primary method Acrobat uses to allow users and admins to specify trusted content that should be exempt from security restrictions, such as when Enhanced Security is enabled.   A Privileged Location may be a file, folder, or a host.  If the user is allowed to set a Privileged Location, they could bypass security protections.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bDisableTrustedFolders == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21312400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bDisableTrustedFolders == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21312400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bDisableTrustedFolders'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\n                        : name equals 'bDisableTrustedFolders'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"73F2A801-6BF7-1014-828A-C38FCC41726B","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213124"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-213124","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":["SV-94079","V-79373"],"group_id_src":"V-213124","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bDisableTrustedFolders\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; 'Privileged folder locations' to 'Disabled'. \n\n"},{"rule_id_src":"SV-213126r766535_rule","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nNote: The Key Name \"cEUTLDownload\" is not created by default in the Acrobat Pro DC install and must be created.\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\Software\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Security\\cDigSig\\cEUTLDownload\n\nValue Name: bLoadSettingsFromURL\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0\n\nIf the value for bLoadSettingsFromURL is not set to â0â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nGUI path: Edit &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; In the 'Automatic European Union Trusted Lists (EUTL) updates' section &gt; Verify the 'Load trusted certificates from an Adobe EUTL server' is not checked.  If the box is checked, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: User Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; 'Load trusted certificates from an Adobe EUTL server' must be set to 'Disabled'.\n","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-213126r766535","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000427","id":"V-213126"},"reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_version":"AADC-CN-000990","severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-APP-000427","ccis":["CCI-002470"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bLoadSettingsFromURL == 0)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21312600 (ntuser_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bLoadSettingsFromURL == 0\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21312600 (ntuser_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Security\\cDigSig\\cEUTLDownload'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bLoadSettingsFromURL'\nExclude Items If        : enabled equals 'false'\nExclude Items If        : days_since_modified is greater than '35'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000021 (ntuser_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Security\\cDigSig\\cEUTLDownload'\n                        : name equals 'bLoadSettingsFromURL'\n                        : sid equals 'S-1-5-21-1196677333-4084102320-1286229203-1001'\n                        : username equals 'WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat'\n                        : account_type equals 'local'\n                        : logged_on equals 'false'\n                        : days_since_last_logon equals '16'\n                        : enabled equals 'true'\n                        : date_modified equals '134331012980000000'\n                        : days_since_modified equals '1'\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Users\\Degthat\\ntuser.dat'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054532480000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous periodic downloading of Adobe European certificates must be disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"By default, the user can update Adobe European certificates from an Adobe server through the GUI.   When updating Adobe European certificates is disabled, it prevents the automatic download and installation of certificates and disables and locks the end user's ability to download those certificates.","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-213126","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":["SV-94083","V-79377"],"group_id_src":"V-213126","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nNote: The Key Name \"cEUTLDownload\" is not created by default in the Acrobat Pro DC install and must be created.\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_CURRENT_USER\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Security\\cDigSig\\cEUTLDownload\n\nValue Name: bLoadSettingsFromURL\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0\n\nConfigure the policy value for User Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; 'Load trusted certificates from an Adobe EUTL server' to 'Disabled'.\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"73F2B7AA-6BF7-1014-BF1B-E0563A2193B1","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213126","href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml"}},{"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bProtectedMode\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for bProtectedMode is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Protected Mode' must be set to 'Enabled'.\n\n","rule_id_src":"SV-213127r766538_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-213127r766538","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-213127","title":"SRG-APP-000431"},"rule_version":"AADC-CN-001010","group_title":"SRG-APP-000431","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-002530"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bProtectedMode == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21312700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bProtectedMode == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21312700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bProtectedMode'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\n                        : name equals 'bProtectedMode'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous Protected Mode must be enabled.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Protected Mode is a âsandboxâ that is essentially a read-only mode.  When enabled, Acrobat allows the execution environment of untrusted PDF's and the processes the PDF may invoke but also presumes all PDFs are potentially malicious and confines processing to a restricted sandbox.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-213127","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":["SV-94085","V-79379"],"group_id_src":"V-213127","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bProtectedMode\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Protected Mode' to 'Enabled'.\n\n\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"73F2C4C0-6BF7-1014-8C81-A28FCAFC0A2B","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213127"}},{"rule_version":"AADC-CN-001015","ccis":["CCI-002530"],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000431","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-213128r766541","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: iProtectedView\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 2\n\nIf the value for iProtectedView is not set to â2â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nGUI path: Edit &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; In the 'Protected View' section, verify the radio button for 'All files' is checked and greyed out (locked). If the button is not checked nor greyed out, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; 'Protected View' must be set to 'Enabled' and 'All files' selected in the drop down box.  \n\n","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213128r766541_rule","reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000431","id":"V-213128"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: iProtectedView\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 2\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; 'Protected View' to 'Enabled' and select 'All files' in the drop down box.  \n","legacy_ids":["SV-94087","V-79381"],"group_id_src":"V-213128","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-213128","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213128","href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml"},"uuid":"73F2D10A-6BF7-1014-8973-B18B8BC8C699","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (iProtectedView == 2)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21312800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : iProtectedView == 2\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21312800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'iProtectedView'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\n                        : name equals 'iProtectedView'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","discussion":"Protected View is a âsuper-sandboxâ that is essentially a read-only mode. When enabled, Acrobat strictly confines the execution environment of untrusted PDF's and the processes the PDF may invoke. Acrobat also assumes all PDFs are potentially malicious and confines processing to a restricted sandbox. When the PDF is opened, the user is presented with the option to trust the document. When the user chooses to trust the document, all features are enabled, this action assigns trust to the document and adds the document to the usersâ list of Privileged Locations.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous Protected View must be enabled."},{"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous latest security-related software updates must be installed.","discussion":"Security flaws with software applications are discovered daily. Vendors are constantly updating and patching their products to address newly discovered security vulnerabilities. Organizations (including any contractor to the organization) are required to promptly install security-relevant software updates (e.g., patches, service packs, and hot fixes). Flaws discovered during security assessments, continuous monitoring, incident response activities, or information system error handling must also be addressed expeditiously. This requirement will apply to software patch management solutions that are used to install patches across the enclave and also to applications that are not part of that patch management solution. For example, many browsers today provide the capability to install their own patch software. Patch criticality, as well as system criticality, will vary. Therefore, the tactical situations regarding the patch management process will also vary. This means that the time period used must be a configurable parameter. Time frames for application of security-relevant software updates may be dependent upon the Information Assurance Vulnerability Management (IAVM) process. The application will be configured to check for and install security-relevant software updates within an identified time period from the availability of the update. The specific time period will be defined by an authoritative source (e.g., IAVM, CTOs, DTMs, and STIGs).","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-213129, SV-213129r400525, SRG-APP-000456)\n","status":"not_reviewed","uuid":"73F2D947-6BF7-1014-97DC-A27B71501D4D","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.acrobatpro:questionnaire:2301"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-213129","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":["V-79383","SV-94089"],"group_id_src":"V-213129","fix_text":"Apply the latest security-related software updates to the Adobe Acrobat Pro DC application.","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"3973","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-213129","title":"SRG-APP-000456"},"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Open Adobe Acrobat Pro DC.\n\nNavigate to and click on Help &gt;&gt; About Adobe Acrobat Pro DC.\n\nVerify that the latest security-related software updates by Adobe are being applied.\n\nIf the latest security-related software updates by Adobe are not being applied, this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-213129r400525_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-213129r400525","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000456","severity":"high","ccis":["CCI-002605"],"rule_version":"AADC-CN-001075"},{"ccis":["CCI-001499"],"severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-APP-000133","rule_version":"AADC-CN-001280","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000133","id":"V-213130"},"reference_identifier":"3973","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213130r766544","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-213130r766544_rule","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bDisablePDFHandlerSwitching\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for bDisablePDFHandlerSwitching is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nGUI path: Edit &gt; Preferences &gt; General &gt; Verify the 'Select As Default PDF Handler' option is greyed out (locked).  If the option is not greyed out, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; General &gt; 'Disable PDF handler switching' must be set to 'Enabled'. \n\n","ia_controls":"","uuid":"73F2E0C1-6BF7-1014-BED3-D844A595C2C8","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213130","href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bDisablePDFHandlerSwitching\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; General &gt; 'Disable PDF handler switching' to 'Enabled'.  \n","group_id":"V-213130","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":["SV-94091","V-79385"],"group_id_src":"V-213130","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous Default Handler changes must be disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Acrobat Pro allows users to change the version of Acrobat Pro that is used to read PDF files. This is a risk if multiple versions of Acrobat are installed on the system and the other version has dissimilar security configurations or known vulnerabilities. When the Default PDF Handler is disabled, the end users will not be able to change the default PDF viewer.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bDisablePDFHandlerSwitching == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21313000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bDisablePDFHandlerSwitching == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21313000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bDisablePDFHandlerSwitching'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\n                        : name equals 'bDisablePDFHandlerSwitching'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213131","href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml"},"uuid":"73F2E7F2-6BF7-1014-AD8A-8991114150FE","legacy_ids":["SV-94093","V-79387"],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-213131","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-213131","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nNote: The Key Name \"cCloud\" is not created by default in the Acrobat Pro DC install and must be created.\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cCloud\n\nValue Name: bDisableADCFileStore\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Store files on Adobe.com' to 'Disabled'.\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC provides the ability to store PDF files on Adobe.com servers. Allowing users to store files on non-DoD systems introduces risk of data compromise.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous must disable the ability to store files on Acrobat.com.","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bDisableADCFileStore == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21313100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bDisableADCFileStore == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21313100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cCloud'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bDisableADCFileStore'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cCloud'\n                        : name equals 'bDisableADCFileStore'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"AADC-CN-001285","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-213131","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"3973","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213131r766547_rule","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nNote: The Key Name \"cCloud\" is not created by default in the Acrobat Pro DC install and must be created.\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cCloud\n\nValue Name: bDisableADCFileStore\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for bDisableADCFileStore is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Store files on Adobe.com' must be set to 'Disabled'.\n\n","ia_controls":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-213131r766547","mitigation_control":""},{"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-213132"},"reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213132r766550_rule","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cServices\n\nValue Name: bTogglePrefsSync\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for bTogglePrefsSync is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Cloud Synchronization' must be set to 'Disabled'.\n\n","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-213132r766550","mitigation_control":"","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"AADC-CN-001290","mitigations":"","discussion":"By default, Adobe online services are tightly integrated in Adobe Acrobat. When the Adobe Cloud synchronization is disabled it prevents the synchronization of desktop preferences across devices on which the user is signed in with an Adobe ID (including phones).","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous Cloud Synchronization must be disabled.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bTogglePrefsSync == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21313200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bTogglePrefsSync == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21313200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cServices'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bTogglePrefsSync'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cServices'\n                        : name equals 'bTogglePrefsSync'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213132"},"uuid":"73F2F024-6BF7-1014-A7FE-BAF12CA0A35E","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":["SV-94095","V-79389"],"group_id_src":"V-213132","group_id":"V-213132","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cServices\n\nValue Name: bTogglePrefsSync\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Cloud Synchronization' to 'Disabled'.\n\n"},{"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-213133","legacy_ids":["SV-94097","V-79391"],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-213133","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nFor 32 bit:\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Installer\n\nFor 64 bit:\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\SOFTWARE\\Wow6432Node\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Installer\n\nValue Name: DisableMaintenance\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Help &gt; 'Repair Installation on 32/64 bit' to 'Disabled'.","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"73F2F80A-6BF7-1014-908D-E098056F45F5","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213133","href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   true (DisableMaintenance == 1)\nTest                    :   true (DisableMaintenance == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21313300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : DisableMaintenance == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21313300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Installer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'DisableMaintenance'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Installer'\n                        : name equals 'DisableMaintenance'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134317141650000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous Repair Installation must be disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"When Repair Installation is disabled the user does not have the option (Help Menu) or ability to repair an Adobe Acrobat Pro DC install. Ability to repair includes the risk that established security settings could be overwritten.","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","rule_version":"AADC-CN-001295","severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id_src":"SV-213133r766553_rule","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: \n\nFor 32 bit:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Installer\n\nFor 64 bit:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Wow6432Node\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Installer\n\nValue Name: DisableMaintenance\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for DisableMaintenance is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nGUI path: Help &gt; Verify the option 'Repair Installation' is greyed out (locked). If the option is not greyed out, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Help &gt; 'Repair Installation on 32/64 bit' must be set to 'Disabled'.\n\n","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-213133r766553","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-213133","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"reference_identifier":"3973","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":""},{"classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-213134r766556","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cServices\n\nValue Name: bToggleWebConnectors\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for bToggleWebConnectors is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Third-party web connectors' must be set to 'Disabled'.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213134r766556_rule","reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-213134"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","rule_version":"AADC-CN-001300","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","severity":"low","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bToggleWebConnectors == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21313400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bToggleWebConnectors == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21313400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cServices'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bToggleWebConnectors'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cServices'\n                        : name equals 'bToggleWebConnectors'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","discussion":"Third-party connectors include services such as Dropbox and Google Drive. When third-party web connectors are disabled, it prevents access to third-party services for file storage. Allowing access to online storage services introduces the risk of data loss or data exfiltration.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous third-party web connectors must be disabled.","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cServices\n\nValue Name: bToggleWebConnectors\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Third-party web connectors' to 'Disabled'.","legacy_ids":["SV-94099","V-79393"],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-213134","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-213134","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213134"},"uuid":"73F308CC-6BF7-1014-8C0F-9225256674F1","status":"not_a_finding"},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","rule_version":"AADC-CN-001305","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-213135"},"reference_identifier":"3973","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213135r766559","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-213135r766559_rule","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cWebmailProfiles\n\nValue Name: bDisableWebmail\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for bDisableWebmail is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'WebMail' must be set to 'Disabled'.","ia_controls":"","uuid":"73F311F8-6BF7-1014-8328-E5897F753325","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213135","href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cWebmailProfiles\n\nValue Name: bDisableWebmail\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'WebMail' to 'Disabled'.","group_id":"V-213135","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":["SV-94101","V-79395"],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-213135","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous Webmail must be disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Acrobat Pro DC provides a Webmail capability. This allows users to send PDFs as email attachments using any mail account that supports SMTP/IMAP protocols. In addition to existing desktop email clients, users can now configure these mail accounts by providing User Name, Password, IMAP and SMTP details. The capability allows users to utilize Gmail and Yahoo mail accounts to send PDF files directly from within the Acrobat application. This capability allows the user to by-pass existing email protections provided by DoD email services.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bDisableWebmail == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21313500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bDisableWebmail == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21313500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cWebmailProfiles'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bDisableWebmail'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cWebmailProfiles'\n                        : name equals 'bDisableWebmail'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213136","href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml"},"uuid":"73F31AAC-6BF7-1014-8571-A849B1FBB3B2","legacy_ids":["SV-94103","V-79397"],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-213136","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-213136","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nNote: The Key Name \"cWelcomeScreen\" is not created by default in the Acrobat Pro DC install and must be created.\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cWelcomeScreen\n\nValue Name: bShowWelcomeScreen\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Welcome Screen' to 'Disabled'.","mitigations":"","discussion":"The Adobe Welcome screen can be distracting. It provides marketing material and also has online links to the Adobe quick tips website, tutorials, blogs, and community forums. When the Adobe Welcome screen is disabled, the Welcome screen will not be populated on application startup.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous Welcome Screen must be disabled.","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bShowWelcomeScreen == 0)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21313600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bShowWelcomeScreen == 0\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21313600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cWelcomeScreen'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bShowWelcomeScreen'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cWelcomeScreen'\n                        : name equals 'bShowWelcomeScreen'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"AADC-CN-001310","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-213136"},"reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213136r766562_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nNote: The Key Name \"cWelcomeScreen\" is not created by default in the Acrobat Pro DC install and must be created.\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cWelcomeScreen\n\nValue Name: bShowWelcomeScreen\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0\n\nIf the value for bShowWelcomeScreen is not set to â0â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'Welcome Screen' must be set to 'Disabled'.","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-213136r766562","mitigation_control":""},{"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-213137"},"reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213137r766565","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-213137r766565_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"NOTE: If configured to an approved DoD SharePoint Server, this is NA.\n\nVerify the following registry configuration:\n\nNote: The Key Name \"cSharePoint\" is not created by default in the Acrobat Pro DC install and must be created.\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cSharePoint\n\nValue Name: bDisableSharePointFeatures\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for bDisableSharePointFeatures is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'SharePoint and Office 365 access' must be set to 'Disabled'.","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","rule_version":"AADC-CN-001315","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous SharePoint and Office365 access must be disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Both SharePoint and Office365 configurations are shared in one setting. Disabling this setting removes the userâs ability to use both SharePoint and Office365 cloud features and functions. If the user is allowed to store files on public cloud services, there is a risk of data compromise.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bDisableSharePointFeatures == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21313700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bDisableSharePointFeatures == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21313700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cSharePoint'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bDisableSharePointFeatures'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cSharePoint'\n                        : name equals 'bDisableSharePointFeatures'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","uuid":"73F32372-6BF7-1014-9A86-AAA2ED9AE4F1","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213137","href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nNote: The Key Name \"cSharePoint\" is not created by default in the Acrobat Pro DC install and must be created.\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\\cSharePoint\n\nValue Name: bDisableSharePointFeatures\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Template &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; 'SharePoint and Office 365 access' to 'Disabled'.","group_id":"V-213137","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-213137","legacy_ids":["SV-94105","V-79399"],"false_positives":""},{"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\Software\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Security\\cDigSig\\cAdobeDownload\n\nValue Name: bLoadSettingsFromURL\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0\n\nIf the value for bLoadSettingsFromURL is not set to â0â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nGUI path: Edit &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; In the 'Automatic Adobe Approved Trust List (AATL) Updates' section &gt; verify the 'Load trusted certificates from an Adobe AATL server' is not checked.  If the box is checked, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: User Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; 'Load trusted certificates from an Adobe AATL server' must be set to 'Disabled'.","rule_id_src":"SV-213138r766568_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-213138r766568","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"3973","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-213138","title":"SRG-APP-000427"},"rule_version":"AADC-CN-001320","group_title":"SRG-APP-000427","severity":"low","ccis":["CCI-002470"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bLoadSettingsFromURL == 0)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21313800 (ntuser_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bLoadSettingsFromURL == 0\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21313800 (ntuser_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Security\\cDigSig\\cAdobeDownload'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bLoadSettingsFromURL'\nExclude Items If        : enabled equals 'false'\nExclude Items If        : days_since_modified is greater than '35'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000021 (ntuser_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Security\\cDigSig\\cAdobeDownload'\n                        : name equals 'bLoadSettingsFromURL'\n                        : sid equals 'S-1-5-21-1196677333-4084102320-1286229203-1001'\n                        : username equals 'WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat'\n                        : account_type equals 'local'\n                        : logged_on equals 'false'\n                        : days_since_last_logon equals '16'\n                        : enabled equals 'true'\n                        : date_modified equals '134331012980000000'\n                        : days_since_modified equals '1'\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Users\\Degthat\\ntuser.dat'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054532480000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n","discussion":"By default, the user can update Adobe certificates from an Adobe server through the GUI. When updating Adobe certificates is disabled, it prevents the automatic download and installation of certificates and disables and locks the end user's ability to download those certificates.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous Periodic downloading of Adobe certificates must be disabled.","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","legacy_ids":["SV-94107","V-79401"],"group_id_src":"V-213138","false_positives":"","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-213138","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_CURRENT_USER\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\Security\\cDigSig\\cAdobeDownload\n\nValue Name: bLoadSettingsFromURL\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0\n\nConfigure the policy value for User Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Trust Manager &gt; 'Load trusted certificates from an Adobe AATL server' to 'Disabled'.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213138","href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml"},"uuid":"73F32CA0-6BF7-1014-8F64-FD2FBB62D0FD"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:02:12\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (bDisableTrustedSites == 1)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21313900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : bDisableTrustedSites == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21313900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'bDisableTrustedSites'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown'\n                        : name equals 'bDisableTrustedSites'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous privileged host locations must be disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Privileged Locations are the primary method Acrobat uses to allow users and admins to specify trusted content that should be exempt from security restrictions, such as when Enhanced Security is enabled.  A Privileged Location may be a file, folder, or a host. If the user is allowed to set a Privileged Location, they could bypass security protections.","stig_uuid":"73F1BA0E-6BF7-1014-A52E-8A2F3B1AC19C","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-213139","legacy_ids":["SV-94109","V-79403"],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-213139","fix_text":"Configure the following registry value:\n\nRegistry Hive:\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path:\n\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bDisableTrustedSites\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; 'Privileged host locations' to 'Disabled'. ","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"73F335B0-6BF7-1014-BCA6-FE99EBD48884","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_Adobe_Acrobat_Pro_DC_Continuous_V2R2_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV2-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.acrobatpro:def:213139"},"rule_id_src":"SV-213139r766571_rule","check_content":"Verify the following registry configuration:\n\nUsing the Registry Editor, navigate to the following: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Adobe\\Adobe Acrobat\\DC\\FeatureLockDown\n\nValue Name: bDisableTrustedSites\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nIf the value for bDisableTrustedSites is not set to â1â and Type is not configured to REG_DWORD or does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nGUI path: Edit &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; In the 'Privileged Locations' section, verify 'Add Host' option is greyed out (locked).  If the option is not greyed out, this is a finding.\n\nAdmin Template path: Computer Configuration &gt; Administrative Templates &gt; Adobe Acrobat Pro DC Continuous &gt; Preferences &gt; Security (Enhanced) &gt; 'Privileged host locations' must be set to 'Disabled'. ","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-213139r766571","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-213139","title":"SRG-APP-000380"},"reference_identifier":"3973","responsib